msgid "Loading.LOADING_TITLE"
msgstr "Loading..."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:0"
msgstr "Tram tracks can be built directly on top of existing roads. No need to redo anything."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:1"
msgstr "If you're running out of space to build, see if you can purchase a new Map Tile!"

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:2"
msgstr "When placing a City Service building, you're shown the service coverage area of existing buildings of the same type."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:3"
msgstr "Outside Connections are any land, sea or air routes out of your city. They handle export, import, and tourist traffic."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:4"
msgstr "Many tools can be used in different modes. Check the bottom left of the screen for options."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:5"
msgstr "Residential zones work best near workplaces."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:6"
msgstr "Commercial zones work best near potential customers."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:7"
msgstr "Industrial zones work best near resources, but also create pollution."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:8"
msgstr "Existing zones can be re-zoned by simply assigning a new zone type on top of the old one."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:9"
msgstr "Reaching new Milestones allows access to new City Services."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:10"
msgstr "By adjusting taxes, you can decide how much residents, companies and industries pay towards the city budget."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:11"
msgstr "The budget for each City Service can be individually adjusted in the City Economy screen."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:12"
msgstr "After each work shift, City Service vehicles need to spend some time out of action for refueling, maintenance, and so on. Some upgrades shorten this period."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:13"
msgstr "In addition to ground level, roads and tracks can also be built on elevated platforms as well as underground."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:14"
msgstr "Freshwater can be pumped from underground deposits as well as from rivers and lakes."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:15"
msgstr "Info Views display information about the city with visual overlays. These help you understand what's happening and where."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:16"
msgstr "Zoned buildings have 5 development levels. Higher level buildings have increased upkeep costs, but also produce less garbage and pollution. They also consume less water and electricity."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:17"
msgstr "Natural disasters may strike the city at random. Warning systems and emergency shelters can help your citizens when that happens. Natural Disasters can also be disabled from the options menu."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:18"
msgstr "Natural resources are used by the local industry. When you have active Agriculture, Forestry, Oil Drilling or Mining industries, other related industries also appear."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:19"
msgstr "Each citizen, vehicle and building can be individually selected. This opens an info panel that shows you more information."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:20"
msgstr "Advanced forms of City Service buildings can be unlocked in the Milestone panel, under their specific development trees."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:21"
msgstr "Keep an eye on Chirper, the social media feed. Your citizens are sure to write when things are going well. Or poorly."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:22"
msgstr "You can pause or speed up the flow of time whenever necessary. The controls are in the bottom left corner of your screen."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:23"
msgstr "Most City Service buildings can be further upgraded after being built. Upgrades enhance the operating capacity of the building or provide additional functionalities."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:24"
msgstr "You can enact Policies to change how certain things in the city function. Citywide policies can be activated on the City Info panel, and district policies from the Info Panels of individual districts."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:25"
msgstr "Weather and traffic cause wear on roads, which leads to lower driving speeds and makes accidents more likely. Road repairs are handled by the Road Maintenance city service."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:26"
msgstr "Access to Medical, Police, and Firefighting helicopters is granted by building the Helipad upgrade on relevant City Service buildings."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:27"
msgstr "Most buildings need a road connection, since roads come with integrated electricity and water infrastructure."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:28"
msgstr "Pay attention to groundwater deposit locations to avoid polluting them when placing industrial zones or fuel burning power plants."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:29"
msgstr "All in-game guidance texts are collected in the Advisor panel in the top right corner of your screen, so you can return to them whenever necessary."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:30"
msgstr "Purchasing new Map Tiles requires both money as well as enough Expansion Permits."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:31"
msgstr "Your Global Theme setting defines the default style of buildings and roads. You can always change this in-game if you wish."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:32"
msgstr "The parallel mode in tool options allows you to build two sets of roads or tracks next to each other."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:33"
msgstr "Existing City Service and Signature buildings can be moved to a new location by opening the building info panel and selecting Relocate."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:34"
msgstr "Electric buses are available through a Bus Depot upgrade."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:35"
msgstr "If you want a City Service to only work inside a certain district, open the building info panel and select Operating Districts."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:36"
msgstr "Pay attention when building water pumping stations. Polluted water will make citizens sick."

#: en
msgid "Loading.HINTMESSAGE:37"
msgstr "The number of turning lanes in an intersection is affected by the road types. Try using asymmetric roads where you need more turning lanes."

