msgid "MapTilePurchase.PURCHASE_STATUS_TOOLTIP[InsufficientPermits]"
msgstr "You don't have enough expansion permits to afford the selected tiles."

#: en
msgid "MapTilePurchase.PURCHASE_STATUS_TOOLTIP[InsufficientFunds]"
msgstr "You don't have enough money to afford the selected tiles."

#: en
msgid "MapTilePurchase.PURCHASE_STATUS_TOOLTIP[InsufficientPermitsInsufficientFunds]"
msgstr "You don't have enough expansion permits nor enough money to afford the selected tiles."

#: en
msgid "MapTilePurchase.PURCHASE_STATUS_TOOLTIP[NoSelection]"
msgstr "You haven't selected any map tiles."

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[PoliciesSectionBuilding]"
msgstr "Activate and deactivate building policies."

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[PoliciesSectionDistrict]"
msgstr "Activate and deactivate district policies."

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[PoliciesSectionCargoRoute]"
msgstr "Activate and deactivate cargo route policies."

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[PoliciesSectionTransportLine]"
msgstr "Activate and deactivate transport line policies."

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[SewageSectionOutlet]"
msgstr "This building pumps sewage into the environment."

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[SewageSectionTreatment]"
msgstr "This building converts sewage back into usable fresh water."

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[SewageSectionTreatmentPurification]"
msgstr "The Purification Rate shows how much of the processed sewage is converted back into fresh water."

#: en
msgid "Main.TOOLTIP_TITLE_DEMAND"
msgstr "Demand"

#: en
msgid "Main.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION_DEMAND"
msgstr "The bars indicate which types of zones are currently needed in your city. The longer the bar, the higher the need for the particular zone. \r\nDemand for zoning fluctuates constantly depending on multiple factors in the constantly evolving city. They are the best indicator of where to focus your building efforts next."

#: en
msgid "ToolOptions.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION[European]"
msgstr "European style architecture."

#: en
msgid "ToolOptions.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION[North American]"
msgstr "North American style architecture."

#: en
msgid "Infoviews.INFOMODE_TOOLTIP[Water Consumption]"
msgstr "The water consumption of a building is determined based on its size and function and, in the case of zoned buildings, its **level**. Higher level buildings consume less water."

#: en
msgid "Infoviews.INFOMODE_TOOLTIP[PipeWater Flow]"
msgstr "Fresh water is delivered into the water network by **Pumping Stations** and **Groundwater Pumping Stations**, and fed to buildings via **Water Pipes**. \r\nThe amount of water in the pipes is displayed as bars of varying lengths."

#: en
msgid "Infoviews.INFOMODE_TOOLTIP[PipeSewage Flow]"
msgstr "Sewage is generated by buildings using fresh water. It is drained by **Sewage Pipes** and expelled out of the water network by **Sewage Outlets** and **Wastewater Treatment Plants**.\r\nThe amount of sewage in the pipes is displayed as bars of varying lengths."

#: en
msgid "Infoviews.INFOMODE_TOOLTIP[Signature Residential]"
msgstr "Signature buildings related to residential zones."

#: en
msgid "Infoviews.INFOMODE_TOOLTIP[Signature Commercial]"
msgstr "Signature buildings related to commercial zones."

#: en
msgid "Infoviews.INFOMODE_TOOLTIP[Signature Industrial]"
msgstr "Signature buildings related to industrial zones."

#: en
msgid "Infoviews.INFOMODE_TOOLTIP[Signature Office]"
msgstr "Signature buildings related to office zones."

#: en
msgid "ToolOptions.TOOLTIP[AutoParent]"
msgstr "Binds overlapping items to a building"

#: en
msgid "ToolOptions.TOOLTIP[LotGrid]"
msgstr "Snap to lot grid"

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[EducationSection]"
msgstr "Studying in a school increases the citizen's **education level**. Higher education makes citizens eligible for new job opportunities as well as further education.\r\n\r\nGraduation times depend on the building **efficiency**, student **well-being**, the **school type**, and some **city-wide effects**.\r\n\r\nDropout rates are dependent on the same factors. In addition, students may decide to quit if the school is too far away, their graduation chance is low, if they are too old or if they can earn more money without a degree over their lifetime."

#: en
msgid "SelectedInfoPanel.TOOLTIP[BatterySection]"
msgstr "Batteries store electricity. They are charged by power plants, and will feed the electric grid when electricity production falls below demand."

